      <p class="eyebrow caption-3">The problem</p>
      <h2 id="problem-title" class="heading-2">A file tree tells you where code lives. Not how it works.</h2>
      <p class="body-3 muted">
        Open an unfamiliar repository and you get an alphabetical list. Nothing in it says which file forty others
        depend on, where the tangled code is, or what nothing calls anymore. So you find out the slow way: open a file,
        follow an import, search, repeat.
      </p>
      <p class="body-3 muted">
        That cost is paid when you join a team, when you review a big change, and again when an AI agent edits
        thirty files while you are away. CodeCity reads the whole repository once and draws the answers, so you look
        first and read second.
      </p>
    </div>
    <img class="split-art" src="/assets/art/art-tree-to-city.webp" width="768" height="768" loading="lazy"
      alt="Illustration of a file tree of folders and files turning into a skyline of lit buildings" />
  </div>
</section>

